WEBVTT

00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:02.079
Data freshness depends entirely on

00:00:02.079 --> 00:00:02.959
the execution path.

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:04.639
Because the AI doesn't know it's

00:00:04.639 --> 00:00:06.599
comparing apples to last week's oranges.

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:09.359
Exactly. If the agent executes a

00:00:09.359 --> 00:00:11.919
direct query against a streaming KQL

00:00:11.919 --> 00:00:14.159
Eventhouse, that temperature data might

00:00:14.159 --> 00:00:15.879
literally be millisecond's old.

00:00:15.899 --> 00:00:17.779
Super fresh. But if it's simultaneously

00:00:17.779 --> 00:00:20.579
querying an imported Power BI model

00:00:20.579 --> 00:00:22.499
for the sales figures, those sales

00:00:22.499 --> 00:00:23.879
figures are only as fresh as

00:00:23.879 --> 00:00:25.619
the last time that specific Power

00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:27.739
BI model was scheduled to refresh.

00:00:28.059 --> 00:00:28.999
So if a job fails.

00:00:29.179 --> 00:00:31.039
If your scheduled refresh failed overnight,

00:00:31.259 --> 00:00:32.779
your data is 24 hours out

00:00:32.779 --> 00:00:34.519
of date. So a non -technical

00:00:34.519 --> 00:00:36.259
executive might look at the chat

00:00:36.259 --> 00:00:38.199
window, see an answer that looks

00:00:38.199 --> 00:00:40.379
completely uniform, highly confident,

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:42.319
and beautifully formatted and have

00:00:42.319 --> 00:00:44.239
absolutely no idea that half the

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:45.899
data informing that sentence is real

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:47.359
time and half is a week

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:48.279
old. That's scary.

00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:49.839
They might make a massive operational

00:00:49.839 --> 00:00:52.219
decision based on a temporal misalignment.

00:00:52.459 --> 00:00:53.919
This is why you cannot blindly

00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:55.819
trust the conversational output in

00:00:55.819 --> 00:00:56.619
the chat interface.

00:00:57.239 --> 00:00:59.099
You or your engineering team must

00:00:59.099 --> 00:01:00.779
rigorously check the source ingestion

00:01:00.779 --> 00:01:02.779
timestamps and verify the reporting

00:01:02.779 --> 00:01:03.200
periods.
